00:28:29.287 --> 00:28:30.120
- [Interviewer] All good?

00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:31.008
- [Photographer] Yeah.

00:28:31.008 --> 00:28:32.820
- [Interviewer] Okay, all right, mate.

00:28:32.820 --> 00:28:34.321
Should we, should we kick--
- Let's do it.

00:28:34.321 --> 00:28:35.764
- [Interviewer] So let's start

00:28:35.764 --> 00:28:38.203
with a bigger picture question.

00:28:38.203 --> 00:28:39.947
Who are your industry heroes,

00:28:39.947 --> 00:28:42.501
'cause you're an industry
hero to a lot of people,

00:28:42.501 --> 00:28:44.564
who--
- Oh, boy.

00:28:44.564 --> 00:28:46.315
This is gonna be a tough one, and so,

00:28:46.315 --> 00:28:48.118
and I'll tell you why,
I don't like the answer,

00:28:48.118 --> 00:28:51.329
but it's the honest answer,
the answer is really nobody.

00:28:51.329 --> 00:28:54.287
And I feel like the
reason I don't like it is,

00:28:54.287 --> 00:28:56.264
when I hear myself even say it,

00:28:56.264 --> 00:28:58.961
there's a level of audacity,
but here's the truth.

00:28:58.961 --> 00:29:03.079
I am a complete byproduct
of a very simple framework.

00:29:03.079 --> 00:29:08.008
My parents are my heroes, and
the consumer is the only thing

00:29:08.008 --> 00:29:10.449
I've ever spent my time on.

00:29:10.449 --> 00:29:14.214
You know, I don't really read
a lot of book, any books,

00:29:14.214 --> 00:29:16.547
I don't consume others, I'm,

00:29:18.438 --> 00:29:22.271
I'm obsessed with
consuming, people consuming.

00:29:23.719 --> 00:29:28.208
So, you know, I admire, or I
could go the other direction,

00:29:28.208 --> 00:29:31.048
I admire anybody who is able to operate

00:29:31.048 --> 00:29:34.712
and sustain a business, because
I know how difficult it is.

00:29:34.712 --> 00:29:35.545
So,

00:29:36.607 --> 00:29:38.786
but that is the truth, it's very ironic,

00:29:38.786 --> 00:29:41.273
because I'm very aware
of, like, what I'm doing

00:29:41.273 --> 00:29:43.781
with my own behavior,
and what it's manifested,

00:29:43.781 --> 00:29:45.151
but I think a lot of that has to do

00:29:45.151 --> 00:29:47.803
with how much I care
about the end consumer.

00:29:47.803 --> 00:29:50.757
And so it's a little meta that way.

00:29:50.757 --> 00:29:52.076
So please, let's make sure the tone

00:29:52.076 --> 00:29:54.072
of that audacious answer is caught,

00:29:54.072 --> 00:29:57.531
because I always struggle
with that question.

00:29:57.531 --> 00:29:58.921
Even the last couple of years, I'm like,

00:29:58.921 --> 00:30:00.934
man, maybe I should start, like,

00:30:00.934 --> 00:30:03.446
paying attention to, but the truth is,

00:30:03.446 --> 00:30:05.219
that is what I spend all my time on,

00:30:05.219 --> 00:30:06.793
which is the end consumer.

00:30:06.793 --> 00:30:11.298
And so the end consumer
is my hero, my obsession,

00:30:11.298 --> 00:30:13.089
what I spend my time on.

00:30:13.089 --> 00:30:14.366
- [Interviewer] Excellent,
okay, and let's talk

00:30:14.366 --> 00:30:17.204
about Singapore, you got,
you're opening up your--

00:30:17.204 --> 00:30:18.037
- Yes.

00:30:18.037 --> 00:30:21.811
- [Interviewer] HQ here in
Singapore, so tell me, you know,

00:30:21.811 --> 00:30:25.372
why Asia, why now, what's
going to be the focus,

00:30:25.372 --> 00:30:28.576
in terms of geography, and
in terms of the products,

00:30:28.576 --> 00:30:31.088
and the clients you're going for?

00:30:31.088 --> 00:30:34.270
- So when I started
VaynerMedia, I had one mission,

00:30:34.270 --> 00:30:38.330
which was to build a global
communications framework

00:30:38.330 --> 00:30:41.013
in the form of a client service business,

00:30:41.013 --> 00:30:45.717
to allow me to take advantage
of global economic downturns,

00:30:45.717 --> 00:30:47.959
and to buy businesses and brands,

00:30:47.959 --> 00:30:52.242
and then run them
through that machine, so.

00:30:52.242 --> 00:30:57.075
Every single part of the world
isn't inevitable, you know,

00:30:58.221 --> 00:31:01.862
the answer to why now is
far more circumstantial

00:31:01.862 --> 00:31:05.244
because I want to be everywhere.

00:31:05.244 --> 00:31:07.767
When and if and how we pop up

00:31:07.767 --> 00:31:11.155
with offices is predicated
a little bit more

00:31:11.155 --> 00:31:14.405
around casting, and in being intuitive,

00:31:15.763 --> 00:31:18.545
and client dynamics, and opportunities.

00:31:18.545 --> 00:31:22.462
So a perfect storm of
Avery and Jeff Nicholson,

00:31:23.412 --> 00:31:26.331
a perfect storm of Risa,
who grew up in the area,

00:31:26.331 --> 00:31:28.151
a perfect storm of me coming out

00:31:28.151 --> 00:31:30.724
and doing some keynotes here
and building up profile,

00:31:30.724 --> 00:31:33.469
a perfect storm of major
Fortune 500 clients

00:31:33.469 --> 00:31:36.229
that we're servicing well
in London and the US asking,

00:31:36.229 --> 00:31:39.747
like, hey, are you in the region?

00:31:39.747 --> 00:31:42.707
Hiring a CFO who spent, you know,

00:31:42.707 --> 00:31:46.723
five to seven years in the
region gave me confidence.

00:31:46.723 --> 00:31:49.134
And then probably in the last half decade,

00:31:49.134 --> 00:31:52.463
the very obvious nature of, okay,

00:31:52.463 --> 00:31:55.706
Asia is, like, forever, like, this is it,

00:31:55.706 --> 00:31:58.613
like, this is gonna be
a very major push, so.

00:31:58.613 --> 00:32:01.806
Macro, inevitable,
micro, circumstance-ion.

00:32:01.806 --> 00:32:03.924
- [Interviewer] Okay, so
it's not just pins in a map,

00:32:03.924 --> 00:32:08.105
really, for you guys, but how
deeply will you, personally,

00:32:08.105 --> 00:32:10.181
be involved in the Asia office?

00:32:10.181 --> 00:32:13.125
I mean, you're a brand within
a brand yourself, right?

00:32:13.125 --> 00:32:16.327
You're probably going to
have to be here fairly often

00:32:16.327 --> 00:32:20.580
for it to make a bang in the
beginning, what's the plan?

00:32:20.580 --> 00:32:23.010
- The plan is, every

00:32:23.010 --> 00:32:25.679
eight to 12 weeks, so I don't
feel like I have to be here

00:32:25.679 --> 00:32:27.012
that, that much.

00:32:28.758 --> 00:32:31.008
I'd prefer to be here more.

00:32:32.575 --> 00:32:34.057
But I'm giving you that answer

00:32:34.057 --> 00:32:35.955
because I think that's
gonna be the actual truth,

00:32:35.955 --> 00:32:39.823
instead of my ideology of every six weeks.

00:32:39.823 --> 00:32:44.573
And so, you know, look, we
service Fortune 500 companies,

00:32:45.412 --> 00:32:48.174
these are global companies,
so a lot of times,

00:32:48.174 --> 00:32:50.809
decisions are being made in other places

00:32:50.809 --> 00:32:53.436
that will impact our business here.

00:32:53.436 --> 00:32:55.826
But I want to be here, in general,

00:32:55.826 --> 00:32:58.928
as a human, I'm interested,
and there's so much going on.

00:32:58.928 --> 00:33:00.011
So, you know,

00:33:01.251 --> 00:33:02.491
I'm gonna be thoughtful about it,

00:33:02.491 --> 00:33:05.397
and then obviously we think a lot about,

00:33:05.397 --> 00:33:07.924
you know, I think a lot
about, what does this mean,

00:33:07.924 --> 00:33:11.987
as a whole, for Mainland
China, Australia, Korea, Japan,

00:33:11.987 --> 00:33:15.621
